  "verbalization": "Neomycin is implicated in the regulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a multi-step mechanism involving the Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. This protein serves as a target for multiple compounds, including 6-Methoxysorigenin and (6aR,11aR)-9-hydroxy-3-methoxy-6a,11a-dihydro-6H-[1]benzofuro[3,2-c]chromene-2-carbaldehyde, which in turn direct the enzyme to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The evidence suggests that neomycin may act through a similar pathway, potentially by modulating the expression or activity of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, thereby influencing the enzyme's function. The overlapping targets and the shared role of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7 in the pathway highlight a possible functional link between neomycin and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, though the exact mechanism by which neomycin exerts its effect remains to be fully elucidated.",
